# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...but the template must be committed: it documents which variables
# exist without carrying any of their values.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Synthetic activity logs for the ML anomaly layer.
#
# Unlike fixtures/inventory.json these are NOT committed. Generation is pure,
# deterministic computation — `npm run logs:gen` rebuilds them byte for byte in
# about 200ms — so committing tens of megabytes of JSON that any checkout can
# reproduce would bloat every clone for nothing. CI regenerates them.
/fixtures/cloudtrail.json
/fixtures/cloudtrail-labels.json

# Detections written by the Python ML layer. Regenerated by `npm run ml:detect`
# from the log above, so committing them would add a large derived file that
# any checkout can rebuild.
/fixtures/anomalies.json

# The Python virtual environment for the ML layer. ml/requirements.txt is the
# committed thing; the tree it installs is disposable and machine-specific.
# Rebuild with `npm run ml:setup`.
/ml/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# TLS material generated by `npm run k8s:up` for the in-cluster database.
#
# SECURITY: k8s/tls/ca.key and k8s/tls/tls.key are private keys. Anyone holding
# the server key can impersonate the database to the dashboard; anyone holding
# the CA key can issue a certificate for any name the deployment trusts. They
# are generated locally, live only here and in a Kubernetes Secret, and are
# regenerated by deleting this directory — so there is never a reason to commit
# them. The certificates beside them are public, but the directory is ignored
# wholesale rather than by extension: an ignore rule that has to be right about
# which file is which is one that eventually is not.
/k8s/tls/
